 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a>
 
-The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The directory is offered in two forms: the browser page readers see, and a machine-readable form of the same list served from a second route — reinstated as a supported surface `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+The directory can be narrowed to only the veterinarians holding a named specialty. The narrowing is requested through the address alone — the page and the machine-readable form each accept a specialty by name, and no visible control is offered in this round. A specialty names a whole entry from the clinic's list and is matched disregarding letter case, not by the beginning of the name. A blank or whitespace-only name narrows nothing, exactly as an empty owner search returns every owner. On the browser page the listing stays paged, and moving between pages keeps the narrowing in force `[REQ-VET-003]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty is named, when either the browser page or the machine-readable route is requested, then the full directory is returned as it is today.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty naming a whole entry from the clinic's list, when the browser page is requested for it, then only the veterinarians holding that specialty are listed, a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the same named specialty, when the machine-readable route is requested for it, then only the veterinarians holding that specialty are returned.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a named specialty differing from a stored specialty only by letter case, when the directory is filtered, then it matches; given a name matching only the start of a specialty, then it does not match.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a name matching no specialty, when either surface is filtered, then the request succeeds with an empty veterinarian list rather than an error.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a blank or whitespace-only specialty, when either surface is requested, then the full directory is returned, as an empty owner search returns every owner.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a filtered browser page with more results than fit one page, when a later page is opened, then that page carries the same specialty and shows only matching veterinarians.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
